course: dictionary
lesson: 6741
title: Omnivores: eaters of everything
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word often gets its meaning from the words beside it. Read this sentence: «Herbivores eat plants, carnivores eat animals, and omnivores eat both.» The three kinds of eater are set side by side, so you can compare them.
explain: The clue is the word «both». Herbivores eat plants and carnivores eat animals, so an omnivore must eat both. Try your meaning in the sentence: "omnivores eat plants and other animals" fits perfectly, so you have understood it.
explain: Now test it on animals you know. «Most bears are omnivores.» Chickens, pigs and raccoons are omnivores too. A cow is a herbivore and a cat is a carnivore, so an omnivore is the animal in the middle.
fact: An omnivore is an animal that eats both plants and other animals.
fact: Informally, an omnivore can also mean a person who eats all kinds of food, including meat and vegetables.
fact: A herbivore eats only plants, and a carnivore eats only meat.
fact: Chickens are omnivores: they eat seeds, worms and insects, and will even eat mice and small frogs.
fact: The adjective is omnivorous, as in an omnivorous diet, which means a diet of both plants and animals.
exercise: «Herbivores eat plants, carnivores eat animals, and omnivores eat both.» What does an omnivore eat? | *Both plants and other animals | Only plants | Only other animals
exercise: Which of these animals is an omnivore? | A cow | *A bear | A cat
exercise: Chickens scratch and peck for seeds, worms and insects. Why are chickens omnivores? | They eat only seeds | They never eat plants | *They eat both plants and animals, such as worms and small frogs
test: «Teeth show what an animal eats: meat-eaters have sharp cutting teeth, plant-eaters flat grinding ones.» Which teeth would suit an omnivore that eats both? | *Teeth that can cope with both plants and meat | Only flat grinding teeth | Only sharp cutting teeth
test: Mia says, "An omnivore is just a hungry animal." What is the best answer? | Yes, any hungry animal is an omnivore | *No, an omnivore is an animal that eats both plants and other animals | No, an omnivore eats only plants
exam: Which word means an animal that eats only plants? | *herbivore | predator | omnivore | carnivore
